<title>PANAMA: Panama stock exchange to get new clearing system.</title>
<headline>Panama stock exchange to get new clearing system.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama's stock exchange will have an electronic clearing system operational next month, Dulcidio de la Guardia, president of Panama's Brokers Association, said.</p>
<p>He told reporters the computerized system, called The Panamanian Clearing and Settlement, Inc (Panaclear), would make transactions more accurate and safer.</p>
<p>Financing was provided by the Inter-American Development Bank through a $2.9 million program to automate stock exchanges throughout Central America.</p>
<p>-- Laurens Grant, Panama City newsroom, 507 2237739</p>
